{"alignments": [{"id": "JOB.25.1.a001", "note": "Waw of the consecutive verb takes the connective the ASV wrote for it, *Then* (rule 14).", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.1.001"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.1.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "JOB.25.1.a002", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.1.002"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.1.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "JOB.25.1.a003", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.1.003"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.1.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "JOB.25.1.a004", "note": "Article on the gentilic takes the written *the* (rule 15).", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.1.004"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.1.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "JOB.25.1.a005", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.1.005"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.1.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "JOB.25.1.a006", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.1.006"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.1.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "JOB.25.1.a007", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.1.007"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.1.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}], "ref": "JOB.25.1", "review_notes": ["Speech-introduction formula; every morpheme has its own English word."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "JOB.25.2.a001", "note": "Infinitive absolute used as a noun; ASV writes *Dominion*.", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.2.001"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.2.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "JOB.25.2.a002", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.2.002"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.2.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "JOB.25.2.a003", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.2.003"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.2.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "JOB.25.2.a004", "note": "Prepositional predicate of a verbless clause takes the construction-supplied copula *are* and heads on the preposition (rule 49).", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.2.004"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.2.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004", "t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "JOB.25.2.a005", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.2.005"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.2.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "JOB.25.2.a006", "note": "Participle with no written subject, rendered by the ASV as a finite verb; the subject pronoun *He* realizes the participle's own masculine-singular person and number and joins its unit under rule 17. Competing reading: *He* as its own `added` unit under rule 25, since the only other morpheme denoting God (the suffix of עִמּוֹ) already holds *him*; the finite-rendering reading was taken because the ASV treats the participle as the clause's verb.", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.2.006"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.2.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007", "t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "JOB.25.2.a007", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.2.007"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.2.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "JOB.25.2.a008", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.2.008"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.2.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "JOB.25.2.a009", "note": "מָרוֹם → *high places* heads on *high* under rule 31, *places* being the supplied generic; discontinuous around the suffix's *his*.", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.2.009"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.2.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012", "t013"], "target_head": "t012"}, {"id": "JOB.25.2.a010", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.2.010"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.2.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011"], "target_head": "t011"}], "ref": "JOB.25.2", "review_notes": ["The *He* of *He maketh* is the one materially contestable unit; see its note."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "JOB.25.3.a001", "note": "Interrogative particle takes the fronted question copula *Is* (rules 17, 50).", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.3.001"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.3.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "JOB.25.3.a002", "note": "Positive existential keeps the presentative frame left after the particle takes *Is*; only *there* remains (rule 50).", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.3.002"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.3.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "JOB.25.3.a003", "note": "Supplied quantifying determiner *any* in a question joins the bare noun's unit and is never the head (rule 15).", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.3.003"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.3.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003", "t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "JOB.25.3.a004", "note": "Possessive לְ rendered *of* (rule 11).", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.3.004"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.3.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "JOB.25.3.a005", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.3.005"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.3.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "JOB.25.3.a006", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.3.006"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.3.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "JOB.25.3.a007", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.3.007"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.3.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "JOB.25.3.a008", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.3.008"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.3.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "JOB.25.3.a009", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.3.009"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.3.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "JOB.25.3.a010", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.3.010"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.3.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012"], "target_head": "t012"}, {"id": "JOB.25.3.a011", "note": "No interrogative particle stands in this clause (מִי has its own *whom*), so the fronted *doth* is the verb's own (rule 17); discontinuous around the negative and subject.", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.3.011"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.3.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011", "t015"], "target_head": "t015"}, {"id": "JOB.25.3.a012", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.3.012"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.3.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t014"], "target_head": "t014"}, {"id": "JOB.25.3.a013", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.3.013"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.3.013", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t013"], "target_head": "t013"}], "ref": "JOB.25.3", "review_notes": [], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "JOB.25.4.a001", "note": "Waw rendered by the connective *then*, read off the ASV (rule 14); postposed after *How*, so the unit is reordered under rule 25.", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.4.001"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.4.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "JOB.25.4.a002", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.4.002"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.4.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "JOB.25.4.a003", "note": "Stative verb rendered *can be just*; modal and copula are auxiliaries, head on the complement *just* (rules 17, 44). The subject noun אֱנוֹשׁ is its own unit.", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.4.003"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.4.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003", "t005", "t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "JOB.25.4.a004", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.4.004"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.4.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "JOB.25.4.a005", "note": "Margin *Or, before* read and set aside; printed *with* governs (rule 38).", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.4.005"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.4.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "JOB.25.4.a006", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.4.006"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.4.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "JOB.25.4.a007", "note": "Waw rendered *Or* (rule 14).", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.4.007"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.4.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "JOB.25.4.a008", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.4.008"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.4.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "JOB.25.4.a009", "note": "*can be clean*, head on the complement *clean*; the *he* belongs to the participial subject, not to this verb, since the ASV writes it as the antecedent of *that is born* (rule 17: an explicit subject takes its own tokens).", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.4.009"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.4.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011", "t013", "t014"], "target_head": "t014"}, {"id": "JOB.25.4.a010", "note": "Anarthrous passive participle used substantivally; the ASV supplies *he that is* to make it a noun phrase, which joins its unit and heads on *born* (rule 46). Discontinuous under rule 25. Competing reading: *he* as the verb's subject pronoun under rule 17 with only *that is born* here; rejected because the participle is the clause's written subject.", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.4.010"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.4.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012", "t015", "t016", "t017"], "target_head": "t017"}, {"id": "JOB.25.4.a011", "note": "Rectum of the construct participle takes *of* (rule 19); supplied *a* is the noun's (rule 15).", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.4.011"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.4.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t018", "t019", "t020"], "target_head": "t020"}], "ref": "JOB.25.4", "review_notes": [], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "JOB.25.5.a001", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.5.001"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.5.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "JOB.25.5.a002", "note": "Extent עַד rendered by a bare *even* with no relational word beside it; the preposition takes the word the ASV spent on it (rule 40 read for the word that is written).", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.5.002"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.5.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "JOB.25.5.a003", "note": "No article morpheme; supplied *the* joins the noun (rule 15).", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.5.003"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.5.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003", "t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "JOB.25.5.a004", "note": "Apodosis waw; the ASV writes no connective for it (rule 14).", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.5.004"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.5.004", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "JOB.25.5.a005", "note": "The ASV recasts the verbal negation as the determiner *no* on the supplied complement; the negative takes the determiner it has become (rule 15).", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.5.005"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.5.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "JOB.25.5.a006", "note": "'shineth' rendered by light verb plus complement *hath ... brightness*; head on the complement carrying the lexeme (rule 44), discontinuous around *no*.", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.5.006"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.5.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005", "t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "JOB.25.5.a007", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.5.007"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.5.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "JOB.25.5.a008", "note": "Supplied *the* joins the noun (rule 15).", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.5.008"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.5.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009", "t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "JOB.25.5.a009", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.5.009"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.5.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012"], "target_head": "t012"}, {"id": "JOB.25.5.a010", "note": "Stative perfect rendered *are ... pure*; head on *pure* (rule 44), discontinuous around *not*.", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.5.010"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.5.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011", "t013"], "target_head": "t013"}, {"id": "JOB.25.5.a011", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.5.011"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.5.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t014"], "target_head": "t014"}, {"id": "JOB.25.5.a012", "note": "עַיִן rendered *sight*; the preposition keeps its own *in*, so no rule 30 fusion.", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.5.012"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.5.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t016"], "target_head": "t016"}, {"id": "JOB.25.5.a013", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.5.013"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.5.013", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t015"], "target_head": "t015"}], "ref": "JOB.25.5", "review_notes": [], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "JOB.25.6.a001", "note": "אַף כִּי is a fixed particle pair rendered by the single expression *How much less*; neither morpheme owns a part of it. Source head on the governing first particle (rule 23); target head on the content word *less* (rule 24).", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.6.001", "WLC.JOB.25.6.002"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.6.001", "status": "noncompositional", "target": ["t001", "t002", "t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "JOB.25.6.a002", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.6.003"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.6.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "JOB.25.6.a003", "note": "The Hebrew writes a verbless predication (man [is] a maggot); the ASV subordinates it to the noun with a supplied relative that no morpheme licenses (rules 46, 55).", "source": [], "source_head": null, "status": "added", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "JOB.25.6.a004", "note": "Nominal predicate takes the construction-supplied copula (rule 20) and its own indefinite article (rule 15).", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.6.004"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.6.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006", "t007", "t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "JOB.25.6.a005", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.6.005"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.6.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "JOB.25.6.a006", "note": "Construct noun takes the supplied *the* (rule 29).", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.6.006"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.6.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010", "t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "JOB.25.6.a007", "note": "Rectum takes *of* (rule 19).", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.6.007"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.6.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012", "t013"], "target_head": "t013"}, {"id": "JOB.25.6.a008", "note": "Second supplied relative over a juxtaposed verbless predication, on the same terms as the first (rules 46, 55).", "source": [], "source_head": null, "status": "added", "target": ["t014"], "target_head": "t014"}, {"id": "JOB.25.6.a009", "note": "Nominal predicate takes the copula and its indefinite article (rules 20, 15).", "source": ["WLC.JOB.25.6.008"], "source_head": "WLC.JOB.25.6.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t015", "t016", "t017"], "target_head": "t017"}], "ref": "JOB.25.6", "review_notes": ["Both *that*s are supplied subordinators over verbless predications the Hebrew juxtaposes to their subjects; the copulas and articles stay with the predicate nouns."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
